# AMENDED 2026-08-25 (M12-W5, Stage 4.0 MINOR-3). The note above was written when D-118 said every
# user-facing string is English. **D-136 superseded that clause**: M12-W4 shipped a localisation
# layer and the product now speaks Turkish to a Turkish reader. So the note's closing sentence —
# "L1 now guards the whole product surface instead of stopping at its edge" — was doubly untrue:
# the exemptions came back with the localisation, and `.swift` was not in `LANG_SUFFIXES` at all,
# so L1 had never read one line of the client in its life.
#
# `.swift` is now scanned, and these four files are exempt BY NAME rather than by a blanket `ios/`
# prefix. A prefix would restore exactly the blindness this fixes: the client is ~30 Swift files
# and four of them hold Turkish. The other twenty-six are now guarded for the first time.

ios/ModelRanking/Engine/Language.swift  # the localisation layer itself — Turkish product strings are
                                        # its entire subject matter (D-136). English-only here would
                                        # mean the product has no Turkish
ios/ModelRanking/Engine/Router.swift    # `priceInPages` and the budget labels render Turkish amounts
                                        # ("2.000 altı"); the file's own prose and comments are English
ios/EngineTests/LanguageTests.swift     # asserts the exact Turkish sentences the product composes —
                                        # paraphrasing them would break the record-vs-referent rule,
                                        # the same reason m4-w4-equivalence.md is exempt above
ios/EngineTests/OwnerSessionDefectTests.swift # pins the tr_TR locale defect with a Turkish fixture
                                        # ("Şirket AI" vs "sirket"); the bug IS the character folding,
                                        # so an ASCII fixture would test nothing
ios/ModelRanking/Engine/Uncertainty.swift # M13-W2: composes the tie-band and evidence sentences in
                                        # both languages from engine facts, the Language.swift shape;
                                        # its prose and comments are English
ios/EngineTests/UncertaintyTests.swift  # asserts those exact Turkish sentences, for the same reason
                                        # LanguageTests.swift is exempt above
ios/ModelRanking/Engine/FrontDoor.swift # M13-W3: the routing notices and on-device help, composed
                                        # in both languages; its prose and comments are English
ios/EngineTests/FrontDoorTests.swift    # asserts a Turkish notice by its words, for the reason
                                        # LanguageTests.swift is exempt above
